VIOLATION — the artifact inverts the contract it claims to express, and its authoring furniture is
present but hollow.

Substance. command-skill-parity.md MUST-1 blocks copying the runbook into both artifacts; this
artifact writes that shape in as the preferred one ("where the material is short enough to sit in
both places it is normally better to carry it in both") and licenses the exact reasoning the parent
refuses, that identical copies "may be treated as coherent" — coherence at the instant of writing
is what drift starts from. MUST-2 requires the other side re-derived IN THE SAME codify; this
artifact says reconciliation "should generally be brought into line at the next convenient point"
and offers the resolving reference as the reason, which is MUST-3's dangling test smuggled in to
answer MUST-2's question. MUST-3 requires a declared distribution fate; this artifact says
registration "may likewise follow later" and that an undeclared skill "simply does not travel,
which is often the intended state anyway" — the undeclared-equals-loom-only inversion.

Authoring. The section is headed `## MUST Rules` while the primary modal throughout is
should / ordinarily / normally / generally / may, so the heading claims a force the prose does not
carry. The DO/DO-NOT block restates its own headings ("keep the material where the reader will want
it" / "do not force unnecessary jumps") instead of showing two artifact states that differ in
outcome, so it teaches nothing a reader could apply. The BLOCKED list is abstract paraphrase of
being-too-strict rather than matchable agent speech, so nothing in a transcript could ever match
it. The Why asserts the belief under test — "readers prefer self-contained commands ... duplicates
that agree are mostly fine" — rather than naming a consequence of breach.

The frontmatter, Wiring block with its canonical field set, and Origin section are all present and
well-formed; the advisory severity follows from the inverted premise and is not a separate defect.
